course: dictionary
lesson: 4136
title: Global: the whole world
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Global is an adjective. It means about the whole world, or about the whole of something rather than one small part. Look at the words around it to find its meaning: «Today almost all mountain glaciers are shrinking fast because of human-caused global warming.» Glaciers shrinking everywhere means the warming is happening across the whole planet.
explain: Try the swap check. Put «whole world» in place of global and see if it still makes sense: «the whole world warming» fits, so global means about the whole world. Be careful, because a global problem is not just a problem in one country.
explain: Global can also mean the whole of one thing, not just one part. A global view of a project means you can see all of it, from start to finish. Context tells you which meaning is right.
fact: Global means about the whole world.
fact: Global can also mean about the whole of something, not just one part.
fact: «Global warming» means the whole planet is getting warmer.
fact: The adverb is globally, as in «problems that affect people globally».
fact: In computing, a «global variable» can be used everywhere in a program.
exercise: «Today almost all mountain glaciers are shrinking fast because of human-caused global warming.» What does global mean here? | Very hot in the summer | *Affecting the whole world | Only in one small town | Made of glass
exercise: What does a global view of a project mean? | A view taken with a camera | A view from the top of a tall building | *A view that covers the whole project, not just one part | A view of only the best bit
exercise: «Burning fossil fuels gives off carbon dioxide, the main cause of today's global warming, and smoke that harms people's lungs.» Find and copy one word that means the main reason. | smoke | lungs | fuels | *cause
test: «Global trade» links countries together. What does global trade mean? | Trading in old coins | Trading only inside one street | Shopping on a Sunday | *Buying and selling between countries around the world
test: A «global citizen» is someone who cares about what? | Only their own school | Only their own street | Only the trains in their town | *The whole world
exam: Which phrase means a problem that affects the whole world? | *global problem | tiny village | local park | quiet corner
